  "question": {
    "text": "A body is moving in a low circular orbit about a planet of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. The radius of the orbit can be taken to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> itself. Then the ratio of the speed of this body in the orbit to the escape velocity from the planet is:&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The orbital velocity of the body in an orbit of the radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>The escape velocity from the surface is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Ratio,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></msqrt><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
